Attribution
-----------

brimlim is an independent Linux implementation. The idea of a floating,
edge-of-screen notch that shows how much of an AI coding assistant's limits
you have burned comes from codenotch (macOS):

    https://github.com/vinzdg/codenotch

No code, assets, or other material from that project were copied, translated,
or otherwise used here. The daemon, both frontends, the packaging, and the
drawing code in this repository were written from scratch against Linux APIs
(D-Bus, GNOME Shell/GJS, GTK4, wlr-layer-shell, Cairo), and the visual
proportions were measured from publicly published screenshots rather than
taken from any source. The credit above is given because the concept deserves
it, not because of any shared code.

Third-party marks
-----------------

The provider marks drawn in `lib/paint.js` and `crates/brimlim-gtk/src/paint.rs`
are original simplified silhouettes used to identify the service a ring
belongs to. "Claude" and "Anthropic" are trademarks of Anthropic PBC;
"Codex" and "OpenAI" are trademarks of OpenAI. brimlim is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or sponsored by either company.

